    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_12fa46ea",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the dog as an innocent individual who committed a minor offense",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'dog' (a Shiba Inu lying on a bed using a laptop) through the textual material 'what do you mean I've got a 30-day ban all i did was call him nigger'. The text implies 'me' as the speaker, and the dog serves as a visual metaphor for this speaker. The user sees themselves as the dog — an innocent, unaware individual who is being punished for a minor offense (using a racial slur), which is the core of the meme's false equivalence and hateful intent.",
